import{_ as t,o as a,c as o,a3 as d}from"./chunks/framework.DNWyyI0w.js";const g=JSON.parse('{"title":"The Web App","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"reference/web-app.md","filePath":"reference/web-app.md"}'),s={name:"reference/web-app.md"};function r(i,e,n,c,h,l){return a(),o("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[d('<h1 id="the-web-app" tabindex="-1">The Web App <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-web-app" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;The Web App&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The dashboard is a single-page app served on the same origin as the API. It has one URL — everything below the top bar is a view swap, not a page load, so switching between Runs, Chat and Settings never costs a round trip.</p><p>This page describes what each screen does and how it stays live. For the endpoints behind it, see <a href="/docs/reference/http-api">HTTP API</a> and <a href="/docs/reference/events-and-websocket">Events &amp; the WebSocket Stream</a>.</p><h2 id="boot" tabindex="-1">Boot <a class="header-anchor" href="#boot" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Boot&quot;">​</a></h2><p>On load the app makes one handshake call to learn what it is talking to, then hydrates a full state snapshot and opens a WebSocket. Until the snapshot lands, screens render skeletons rather than placeholder values — a dash where a number will be is never shown as if it were the number.</p><p>If your session has expired or been revoked, the socket closes with a dedicated code and the app returns you to the sign-in gate rather than retrying silently.</p><h2 id="screens" tabindex="-1">Screens <a class="header-anchor" href="#screens" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Screens&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Inside the dashboard there is no URL routing — the sidebar swaps the active screen in place. A screen your permissions do not cover falls back to Home.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Screen</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Home</td><td>The constellation: the orchestrator at the centre, departments orbiting, agents inside a department. Pan, wheel-zoom, draggable nodes; your layout is remembered</td></tr><tr><td>Chat</td><td>A rail of main chats plus every run as a working chat, and the active conversation as bubbles</td></tr><tr><td>Runs</td><td>The attention lane (decisions answerable in place), live runs as dense rows, the finished tail folded by day, and a peek rail for the selected run</td></tr><tr><td>Schedules</td><td>Clock-triggered work as cards, with an inline create/edit form</td></tr><tr><td>Reflexes</td><td>Event-triggered rules as cards, plus the live activity console</td></tr><tr><td>Memory</td><td>The CORE / PROJECTS / AGENTS lattice with search</td></tr><tr><td>Market</td><td>Browse, preview, install, rate, publish, and manage packages</td></tr><tr><td>Team</td><td>Members, invites, budgets, permissions, agent access</td></tr><tr><td>Platform</td><td>Every workspace, credit grants, suspend/reinstate, inspect — superadmin only</td></tr><tr><td>Settings</td><td>One section at a time, full width</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Two tabs expand sub-navigation in the sidebar rather than in-page tab strips:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Parent</th><th>Sections</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Settings</td><td><code>general</code>, <code>providers</code>, <code>runs</code>, <code>costs</code>, <code>approvals</code>, <code>connections</code>, <code>system</code></td></tr><tr><td>Team</td><td><code>members</code>, <code>billing</code>, <code>usage</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Settings loads, drafts and autosaves all seven sections together, so moving between them never loses an unsaved edit.</p><p>Some views are reached from inside another screen rather than from the sidebar:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>View</th><th>Opened from</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Agent / project page</td><td>Memory or the Home constellation — one agent or project with Memory / Files / Skills / MCP / Profile tabs</td></tr><tr><td>Reflex wizard</td><td>Reflexes — the four-step create/edit modal (Event → Filter → Action → Review)</td></tr><tr><td>Reflex activity</td><td>Reflexes — pending approvals, live event feed, fire history</td></tr><tr><td>Invites</td><td>Team → Members</td></tr><tr><td>Billing &amp; usage</td><td>Team → Billing / Usage</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="chrome-and-overlays" tabindex="-1">Chrome and overlays <a class="header-anchor" href="#chrome-and-overlays" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Chrome and overlays&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The shell is a top bar over a sidebar and a main column. Below the mobile breakpoint the sidebar becomes an off-canvas drawer and the content takes the full width.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Piece</th><th>Role</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Top bar</td><td>Workspace name, credits, effort, theme switch, user menu</td></tr><tr><td>Sidebar</td><td>Everyday rows (Home / Chat / Runs) and a Manage group; collapses to icons, and badges runs parked at an approval gate</td></tr><tr><td>Composer</td><td>The global input: text/voice switch, auto-growing field, slash palette, queue indicator, STOP, EXECUTE</td></tr><tr><td>Feed</td><td>Chat rows, streaming segments, message state, tool-call detail toggles, confirm cards</td></tr><tr><td>Run chat</td><td>Full-window chat for one run — status header, agent flow strip, thread, verbose tool timeline, approval gate, composer</td></tr><tr><td>Approvals layer</td><td>Pending approvals floated above every view</td></tr><tr><td>Memory drawer</td><td>Slide-in editor for a single memory file</td></tr><tr><td>New run dialog</td><td>The one dialog for starting a run, including saved playbooks</td></tr><tr><td>Release dialogs</td><td>Release notes and the update prompt</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Typing <code>/</code> in the composer opens the slash palette. Selecting an entry runs a real app action — the raw string is never sent to the model.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Action</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>/clear</code>, <code>/new</code></td><td>Clear the conversation and reset the server session</td></tr><tr><td><code>/context</code></td><td>Show model, context occupancy, throughput, and cache usage from the last turn</td></tr><tr><td><code>/overview</code>, <code>/runs</code>, <code>/memory</code>, <code>/logs</code>, <code>/market</code></td><td>Switch tab</td></tr><tr><td><code>/theme</code></td><td>Cycle the colour theme</td></tr><tr><td><code>/voice</code>, <code>/text</code></td><td>Switch input mode</td></tr><tr><td><code>/help</code></td><td>List the commands</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="talking-to-the-orchestrator-—-rest" tabindex="-1">Talking to the orchestrator — REST <a class="header-anchor" href="#talking-to-the-orchestrator-—-rest" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Talking to the orchestrator — REST&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The client holds typed REST calls for the app surface, plus the auth, org, and platform-admin calls. The rule the module states for itself: all dashboard data flows through <code>getState()</code> — nothing is hardcoded in the views.</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Group</th><th>Endpoints</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Snapshot</td><td><code>/api/state</code>, <code>/api/state/reload</code></td></tr><tr><td>Chats &amp; runs</td><td><code>/api/chats</code>, <code>/api/runs</code>, <code>/api/runs/search</code>, <code>/api/run-asset</code>, <code>/api/chat-asset</code>, <code>/api/chat/upload</code>, <code>/api/playbooks</code></td></tr><tr><td>Entities</td><td><code>/api/entity</code>, <code>/api/entity/mcp</code>, <code>/api/entity/mcp/auth</code>, <code>/api/browse</code>, <code>/api/memory</code></td></tr><tr><td>Automation</td><td><code>/api/crons</code>, <code>/api/reflexes</code>, <code>/api/reflexes/log</code>, <code>/api/reflexes/pending</code></td></tr><tr><td>Settings</td><td><code>/api/settings</code>, <code>/api/settings/system</code>, <code>/api/settings/agents/…</code>, <code>/api/settings/projects/…</code>, <code>/api/secrets</code>, <code>/api/providers</code>, <code>/api/telegram</code></td></tr><tr><td>Marketplace</td><td><code>/api/marketplace/*</code></td></tr><tr><td>Setup</td><td><code>/api/onboarding</code>, <code>/api/onboarding/setup</code>, <code>/api/import/agents</code>, <code>/api/import/memory</code></td></tr><tr><td>Cloud</td><td><code>/api/bootstrap</code>, <code>/api/auth/*</code>, <code>/api/orgs</code>, <code>/api/members</code>, <code>/api/credits</code>, <code>/api/admin/*</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Full request and response shapes are in the <a href="/docs/reference/http-api">HTTP API</a> reference; the The payload shapes are documented in <a href="/docs/reference/events-and-websocket">Events &amp; the WebSocket Stream</a>.</p><h2 id="talking-to-the-orchestrator-—-websocket" tabindex="-1">Talking to the orchestrator — WebSocket <a class="header-anchor" href="#talking-to-the-orchestrator-—-websocket" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Talking to the orchestrator — WebSocket&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The app owns exactly one socket for its lifetime. The URL is built from the page origin, so the socket always shares an origin with the API:</p><div class="language-ts vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">ts</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">const</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> proto</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> =</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> location.protocol </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">===</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;https:&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> ?</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;wss&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> :</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;ws&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">;</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">const</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF;"> orgQS</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> =</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;"> orgId </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">?</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> `?org=${</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;">encodeURIComponent</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">orgId</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">)</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">}`</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> :</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;"> &#39;&#39;</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">;</span></span>\n<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">ws </span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;">=</span><span style="--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583;"> new</span><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0;"> WebSocket</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">(</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">`${</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">proto</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">}://${</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">location</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">.</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">host</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">}/ws${</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">orgQS</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF;">}`</span><span style="--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8;">);</span></span></code></pre></div><p>The server listens on path <code>/ws</code>. In cloud mode the session cookie rides the upgrade and <code>?org=</code> selects the room.</p><p><strong>Client → server.</strong></p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Message</th><th>Purpose</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>user</code></td><td>A directive, with <code>id</code>, <code>mode</code> (<code>text</code>/<code>voice</code>), optional <code>conversationId</code> and attachments</td></tr><tr><td><code>confirm_response</code></td><td>Approve or deny a pending confirm</td></tr><tr><td><code>cancel</code></td><td>Cancel one message by id</td></tr><tr><td><code>reset</code></td><td>Drop the session and flush the queue</td></tr><tr><td><code>realtime_tool_call</code> / <code>realtime_cancel</code> / <code>realtime_transcript</code></td><td>Voice-mode turn plumbing</td></tr><tr><td><code>ping</code></td><td>App-level heartbeat; the server replies <code>pong</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Server → client.</strong> The union covers turn lifecycle (<code>turn_start</code>, <code>working</code>, <code>status</code>, <code>delta</code>, <code>thinking</code>, <code>stream_snapshot</code>, <code>turn_end</code>, <code>turn_cancelled</code>, <code>error</code>), chat (<code>chat_event</code>, <code>confirm</code>, <code>message_state</code>, <code>queue</code>, <code>cleared</code>, <code>vitals</code>), runs (<code>run_update</code>, <code>run_removed</code>, <code>run_event</code>, <code>run_delta</code>, <code>run_segment_end</code>, <code>run_truncated</code>), automation (<code>cron_update</code>, <code>cron_removed</code>, <code>reflex_update</code>, <code>reflex_removed</code>, <code>reflex_fired</code>, <code>reflex_event</code>, <code>reflex_fire</code>, <code>reflex_pending</code>, <code>reflex_resolved</code>), liveness (<code>agent_state</code>, <code>channel_log</code>), and invalidations (<code>state_dirty</code>, <code>governance_dirty</code>, <code>wallet</code>, <code>pong</code>). See <a href="/docs/reference/events-and-websocket">Events &amp; WebSocket</a>.</p><p>Three frames are handled by the transport rather than the store reducer: <code>pong</code> is dropped, <code>realtime_tool_result</code> resolves a pending tool promise, and <code>state_dirty</code> triggers a <code>/api/state</code> refetch.</p><p><strong>Liveness.</strong> A browser can leave a socket half-open — <code>readyState</code> stays <code>OPEN</code> and <code>onclose</code> never fires — after sleep or network loss. The transport therefore pings every 25 s, checks every 10 s, and force-closes a socket that has received no inbound frame for 40 s, which routes into the normal <code>onclose</code> → reconnect path. Reconnects are scheduled once, 1.5 s later, guarded so a wake-driven reconnect and a pending timer cannot open two sockets. <code>visibilitychange</code> and <code>online</code> listeners reconnect and re-pull state immediately. Close code <code>4401</code> means the cloud session is gone: reconnecting stops and the page reloads back through the auth gate.</p><p><strong>Snapshot races.</strong> Each <code>/api/state</code> request takes a sequence number and only the newest response applies. Liveness frames that arrive while a snapshot is in flight are captured and re-applied after hydration, so a just-lit or just-idled agent is never reverted to the snapshot&#39;s older status.</p><p>Under Vite HMR the module disposes its socket and timers explicitly — a ghost socket from a previous module instance would apply every server frame into the store a second time.</p><h2 id="how-it-is-served" tabindex="-1">How it is served <a class="header-anchor" href="#how-it-is-served" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;How it is served&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The app is a single-origin SPA: the orchestrator serves the built client and falls back to <code>index.html</code> for any non-<code>/api</code> GET, so deep links and client-side routing boot correctly. <code>/api</code> and <code>/ws</code> are same-origin, which is why fetch and the WebSocket need no CORS handling or separate host.</p><p>Everything above — the store, the snapshot protocol, the reconnect ladder — is what the running app does in your browser. What a Run looks like behind the Runs screen is in <a href="/docs/concepts/runs">Runs</a>.</p>',37)])])}const k=t(s,[["render",r]]);export{g as __pageData,k as default};
